.SH NAME
VTTRegion.id \- VTTRegion: id property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]id\f[B]\f[R] property of the \f[CR]VTTRegion\f[R]
interface is a string that identifies the region.
.SH VALUE
A string that identifies the region.
Initialized to an empty string when the \f[CR]VTTRegion\f[R] object is
first constructed.
.SH EXAMPLES
In the following example, a new \f[CR]VTTRegion\f[R] is created, then
the value of \f[CR]id\f[R] is set to \f[CR]\(dqregion1\(dq\f[R].
The value is then printed to the console.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] region = \f[B]new\f[R] VTTRegion();
region.id = \(dqregion1\(dq;
console.log(region.id);
.EE
